Neapolitan is a Romance language spoken across much of southern Italy and, despite what one may think, It has specific syntactic and grammar rules to form sentences. It is a local dialect, so it is mainly a spoken language, and has had an international impact for many reasons.

As for the other languages I teach, for Neapolitan I propose a customized learning program to help you master the basics of this wonderful dialect, including the study of gestures and Neapolitan culture. 

I will teach you:
•	how to introduce and speak about yourself;
•	important notions about Neapolitan gestures and culture;
•	basic grammar, vocabulary and pronunciation;
•	real-life language and idioms;

Also, I provide my students with plenty of examples, audiovisual resources and exercise to ensure the concepts are clearly understood.

Studying Neapolitan means much more than mastering a new language!
It is about mastering your emotions!

